ows traffic from a sub range  10.10  zero forward slash 24 to avoid such  incidents in the future you want to  proactively clean up your firewall  configurations and automatically  identify all firewall rules accidentally  overshadowed by other rules firewall  insights and Network intelligence Center  provides you with a convenient list of  rules overshadowed by other firewall  rules a rule can be either overshadowed  by a single or a combination of multiple  rules in this case the rule allowing  traffic on both port 8080 and 443 is  overshadowed by a combination of to deny  rules blocking HTTP and HTTPS traffic  respectively you can review each  shadowed role in site detail and adjust  the rule settings to match your  application traffic control needs in  this second scenario I'll show you the  allowed rules with no hit insight to  help you clean up your allow rules  leftover from past projects and tighten  up your security boundaries to find out  what these unnecessary allowed rules are  I'll go to the firewall insights in the  network intelligence Center on the allow  rules with no hit card I see a list of  firewall rules that I have not been hit  by any traffic in the last six weeks we  notice that there is a rule for allowing  Internet traffic to an app in a test  project web app one that the project  owner forgot to clean up the firewall  insights module automatically detects  such leftover allowed rules so that you  can get the opportunity to clean it up  using firewall insights you can not only  identify problems in your firewall rule  configuration but also obtain visibility  into abnormal traffic patterns that you  want to get alerted to deny roll with  hits helps you capture the traffic  blocked by the deny rules and detect  external attacks or misbehaving VMs in  your cloud deployment from the list you  can easily drill down to the  corresponding firewall logs to review  and find out where the denied traffic  came from in summary firewall insights  automatically detects overlapping and  misconfigured rules to help you maintain  the right set of firewall rules that  protect your cloud deployment and brings  real-time visibility to your firewall  utilization statistics  you  [Music]

